OL,3,GNEWSACouncil considers #400 charge for
OL,4,Awhite lines
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council is considering introducing a
OL,7,F#400 charge for residents who want
OL,8,FH-bar road markings painted outside
OL,9,Ftheir homes.
OL,11,FThe white lines, which look like an
OL,12,Felongated H, are advisory and not
OL,13,Flegally enforceable, and are often used
OL,14,Fto discourage parking near dropped
OL,15,Fkerbs and driveways.
OL,17,FLincolnshire Council Council, which
OL,18,Fcurrently funds the markings itself at
OL,19,Fa cost of about #25,000 a year, said
OL,20,Fthe proposed fee would cover
OL,21,Finstallation and administration costs.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
